Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Basic Examples", "Subsection",
 Editable->True,
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->904125756,ExpressionUUID->"8ad9d452-2e30-4456-a46b-e0afaf4735f7"],

Cell["\<\
By default  plain multivector representation is used, which is convenient for \
input and is versatile for large class of manipulations.   The plain form, \
however, expansion of geometric products is slow, also this internal \
representation form is not convenient for operations like component  or grade \
projection and sorting.  For these operations it is better to change internal \
MV representation form to association. To demonstrate interplay of both \
representations, we define algebra basis\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.962440334662866*^9, 3.962440900865793*^9}},
 CellID->1171172506,ExpressionUUID->"6866c76f-ac71-47ba-960e-c6c940ff49b6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

